{"book":19,"chapter":137,"context":{"chapter":137,"title":"By the Rivers of Babylon","summary":"Exiles weep beside Babylon's rivers, refuse their captors' demand for a song of Zion, swear never to forget Jerusalem, and call for judgment on Edom and Babylon.","background":"No title. It comes from the Babylonian exile after 586 BC. Babylon was laced with the Euphrates and irrigation canals (Ezekiel 1:1). Edom cheered Jerusalem's fall (Obadiah 1:10-14). The shocking final verse reflects the brutal warfare of the time, when conquerors dashed children against stones (Nahum 3:10); the exiles voice their anguish to God rather than act on it.","customs":[{"term":"Harps on the willows","verses":"137:2","note":"The trees were probably poplars by the water. Hanging up the lyres meant refusing to perform."}],"watchFor":["'How shall we sing the LORD's song in a strange land?' (v. 4).","The musician's self-curse on hand and tongue (vv. 5–6)."],"connections":["Obadiah 1:10-14","Ezekiel 1:1","Lamentations 4:21-22","Jeremiah 51:24"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["עַל","'al","H5921","HR","at"],["נַהֲרוֹת","naharot","H5104","HNcfpc","[the] rivers of"],["בָּבֶל","bavel","H894","HNpl","Babylon"],["שָׁם","sham","H8033","HD","there"],["יָשַׁבְנוּ","yashavnu","H3427","HVqp1cp","we sat"],["גַּם","gam-","H1571","HD","also"],["בָּכִינוּ","bakhinu","H1058","HVqp1cp","we wept"],["בְּזָכְרֵנוּ","bezakherenu","H2142","HR/Vqcc/Sp1bp","when remembered we"],["אֶת","'et-","H853","HTo","<obj.>"],["צִיּוֹן","tziyon","H6726","HNpl","Zion"]],"x":[[26001001,26001001,9],[26003015,26003015,6],[25002010,25002011,4],[25002018,25002018,4],[25003048,25003048,4],[26001003,26001003,4],[15008021,15008021,3],[15008031,15008031,3],[16001003,16001004,3],[16002003,16002003,3]],"xn":18},"2":{"w":[["עַל","'al-","H5921","HR","on"],["עֲרָבִים","'aravim","H6155","HNcmpa","poplars"],["בְּתוֹכָהּ","betokhah","H8432","HR/Ncmsc/Sp3fs","in [the] midst of it"],["תָּלִינוּ","talinu","H8518","HVqp1cp","we hung up"],["כִּנֹּרוֹתֵינוּ","kin